WEBVTT

NOTE
Disc 1, Scene 33h: The Lunar Cry — End of Disc 2
Duration: ~1:22 (82 seconds)
Source: FF8 Gameplay/Cutscene
Describes the catastrophic Lunar Cry event — an apocalyptic phenomenon triggering a massive influx of monsters from the moon to the planet

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The lunar surface is revealed in full. The camera pans across a vast, barren landscape of gray rock and countless craters. The surface appears lifeless and empty. But then — movement. A subtle tremor across the terrain.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The truth becomes apparent. The entire lunar surface is covered with monsters. Millions upon millions of creatures densely packed together, shoulder to shoulder, covering every visible inch of ground. The sheer scale is incomprehensible — a living ocean of beasts.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
The Lunar Cry begins. A massive column of red energy erupts from the lunar surface, streaking downward toward the planet below. The energy beam is enormous — hundreds of kilometers in diameter. It crackles and pulses with power. The beam cuts through space, a weapon of planetary scale.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The monsters pour into the energy beam like water down a drain. Millions of creatures are caught in the flow, swept up in the torrent of power. They fall — an endless cascade of beasts descending toward the planet. The scale is apocalyptic and incomprehensible.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The camera follows the stream of monsters as they descend through space toward the planet. The creatures tumble through the void — all types and sizes, an army without end. The beam of energy carries them along, accelerating them toward the world below.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The planet's upper atmosphere is breached. The monsters enter the sky, streaking downward like a meteor shower — but instead of harmless rocks, an invasion force. They enter the atmosphere, burning with friction, leaving trails of light across the sky.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The Lunar Base, caught in the chaos of the Cry, begins to experience catastrophic damage. The station shakes violently. Debris floats in the corridor. Emergency lights flash red. Alarms sound. The base's structural integrity is compromised.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The Lunatic Pandora is visible from the base — a massive crystal pillar structure, perhaps a prism or conduit. It gleams with terrible power, glowing with the same red energy as the Lunar Cry. The structure triggered this cataclysm.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Inside the Lunar Base, chaos reigns. The team is scattered by the violent shaking. Squall struggles to maintain his footing as the station falls apart around him. Panels explode. Sparks fly from damaged systems. The base is a death trap.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The camera returns to the outside view. The Lunar Base is visibly breaking apart. Modules separate from the main structure. Solar panels tear loose. The base falls toward the moon or tumbles into space — its fate sealed.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
The stream of monsters continues relentlessly. They pour down toward the planet in an endless torrent. The scale of the invasion is beyond comprehension — more creatures than could ever be counted, more enemies than could ever be fought.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The Lunar Base descends further. The station's death is imminent. The team's fate hangs in the balance. Squall's determination flashes across his face — he will not give up, even as everything falls apart around him.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The final moments. The Lunar Cry continues. The planet below is about to be engulfed by millions of monsters falling from the sky. The Base breaks apart completely. Sections tumble away into the void. The scene cuts to black as the full impact of the catastrophe becomes clear.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Silence and darkness. The Lunar Cry has been unleashed. Disc 2 ends with the world teetering on the brink of destruction and the fate of Squall, Rinoa, and the world itself uncertain.
